    <name>
      <text>Derivative of a Given Function_LTM</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Find the derivative of \(f(x) = {@fx@}\).</p><p>\(f'(x)=\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution</b></p>
<p>To find the derivative of the function \(\displaystyle  f(x) \), we can apply the power rule. </p>
<p>Given \( \displaystyle g(x) = ax^n\), where \(a\) and \(n\) are constants, \( \displaystyle g'(x) = nax^{n-1}\).</p>
<p>  Therefore,
\[
\displaystyle
\begin{align*}
f'(x) &= \frac{d}{dx}({@fx@}) \\
&= {@ p1@}x^{({@p1@}-1)}+{@c2*p2@}x^{({@p2@}-1)}+{@c3*p3@} x^{({@p3@}-1)}+{@c4*p4@} x^{({@p4@}-1)}  \\
&= {@ta@}.
\end{align*}
\]
</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
